WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:09.555
Bitsy's button waits for a press. Its
two sensors wait for nothing at all.

2
00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:13.536
Add a loop, and Bitsy runs
round and round all by itself.

3
00:00:14.036 --> 00:00:18.773
Bitsy has five inputs. Button A,
a shake sensor and a microphone.

4
00:00:18.993 --> 00:00:22.709
Then two more: a temperature
sensor and a light sensor.

5
00:00:22.929 --> 00:00:28.455
A sensor is an input that senses
by itself. Nobody presses a sensor.

6
00:00:28.675 --> 00:00:33.969
The temperature sensor feels how warm it
is. The light sensor sees how bright it is.

7
00:00:34.189 --> 00:00:37.997
So a program starts with when
the sensor senses something.

8
00:00:38.497 --> 00:00:41.887
When it gets hot, turn
the motor, show a smile.

9
00:00:42.107 --> 00:00:46.287
That is a fan that starts
itself. Nobody pressed anything.

10
00:00:46.507 --> 00:00:49.943
When it gets dark, all lights
on, beep. That is a night light.

11
00:00:50.163 --> 00:00:55.225
The when block names the input. Press
A, and this program does nothing.

12
00:00:55.725 --> 00:01:00.323
A repeat block repeats the output
after it, a counted number of times.

13
00:01:00.543 --> 00:01:06.255
When A is pressed, repeat 3 times,
beep. Count them: one, two, three.

14
00:01:06.475 --> 00:01:10.608
Then it stops on its own. That
is a count-controlled loop.

15
00:01:10.828 --> 00:01:17.098
A forever block repeats everything after
it. Lights on, wait, lights off, wait.

16
00:01:17.318 --> 00:01:21.218
Round and round, a flashing
light, until you press Stop.

17
00:01:21.718 --> 00:01:27.059
A control system senses something,
decides with a program, and acts.

18
00:01:27.279 --> 00:01:30.762
A thermostat senses the cold
and turns the heating on.

19
00:01:30.982 --> 00:01:35.951
A street lamp senses the dark and
lights up. Nobody flicks a switch.

20
00:01:36.171 --> 00:01:39.515
A greenhouse senses the
heat and opens its window.

21
00:01:39.735 --> 00:01:44.147
Bitsy's night light does all
three: sense, decide, act.

22
00:01:44.647 --> 00:01:50.034
A candle, a pencil, a bicycle.
Nothing senses and nothing decides.

23
00:01:50.254 --> 00:01:53.272
A radio you switch on by
hand is not one either.

24
00:01:53.492 --> 00:01:57.718
A person decides every time.
There is no program in the middle.

25
00:01:57.938 --> 00:02:01.746
A control system decides
by itself, from a sensor.

26
00:02:02.246 --> 00:02:07.169
Look closely at Bitsy's screen. It is
twenty-five little lights in a grid.

27
00:02:07.389 --> 00:02:09.943
Count them: five across and five down.

28
00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:15.039
Each little light is an LED.
An LED uses very little power.

29
00:02:15.259 --> 00:02:18.696
Show a heart switches some LEDs
on and leaves the rest off.

30
00:02:18.916 --> 00:02:23.374
A real board called the micro:bit
has the same grid of LEDs.

31
00:02:23.594 --> 00:02:27.402
You program it in MakeCode, and
its blocks do what yours do.

32
00:02:27.902 --> 00:02:31.385
A sensor senses by itself.
It never needs a press.

33
00:02:31.605 --> 00:02:37.642
A repeat loop counts, then stops.
A forever loop runs until Stop.

34
00:02:37.862 --> 00:02:42.413
Bitsy's screen is twenty-five
LEDs, switched on by your program.

35
00:02:42.633 --> 00:02:48.392
Sense, decide, act. That is a control
system, and it is all around you.
